# .dockerignore — what must never enter the Docker build context.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS A SECURITY CONTROL AND NOT HOUSEKEEPING. The Dockerfile's
# final image is clean by construction: it is distroless and only the compiled
# binary is copied forward. The BUILD STAGE is not. `COPY . .` copies whatever
# the build context holds, and a working tree of this project holds the
# operator's live config.yml — one api_key per *arr — plus a .env, the whole
# .git history, and agent scratch.
#
# A build-stage layer is not private. It survives in the BuildKit cache on
# whatever host ran the build, and it is directly readable with
# `docker build --target build`, `docker buildx ... -o type=local`, or
# `docker history` on the cached stage. Since this project is built on the
# machine it is deployed to, an unfiltered context means `docker build` copies
# the developer's *arr credentials onto the server as a side effect — the exact
# thing that never appears in any log, any commit, or any image manifest, and
# so is never noticed.
#
# The list below is the .gitignore list, and container_test.go asserts that it
# STAYS the .gitignore list: anything git is told to refuse must be refused
# here too, or the next secret file added to this repo is protected from the
# remote and handed straight to Docker.

# Private planning docs
cutoffarr-implementation-plan.md

# Local config / secrets. config.yml is the live one: it carries a real api_key
# for every configured instance. The image reads its config from the mounted
# /config volume at RUN time; nothing about the build needs it.
config.yml
config.yaml
*.env
.env*

# Build artifacts. /cutoffarr is a host-built binary — the wrong GOOS/GOARCH for
# the image, ~9 MB, and rebuilt inside the build stage anyway.
/cutoffarr
*.exe
dist/
bin/

# Agent scratch
.superpowers/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Git's own directory, which .gitignore has no reason to name and this file
# does: every key ever committed by mistake and later removed is still in here.
# The build needs no version information (-trimpath, and no ldflags read git).
.git
